                "reply_count": 3,
                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Health care affordability remains one of the most pressing challenges facing American families. Lowering health care costs will require real reform, not more subsidies to insurance companies that only mask costs while nothing to bring them down for everyone else. Real affordability can only come from restoring competition, transparency, and choice. The Lower Health Care Premiums for All Americans Act, which passed the House last week with my strong support, is an important step in that direction. \n\nAmerican families deserve high-quality, affordable health care, and I will continue fighting to ensure they have it. Read more in my op-ed here: https://t.co/TtjuLFoZkU",
